---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { REPO_URL, suggestCommandUrl } from '../lib/github';

const TLDR = 'https://github.com/tldr-pages/tldr';
const CC_BY = 'https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/';
---

<Base title="About" description="What GrepMeIfYouCan is, where its commands come from, and how to contribute.">
  <header class="page-head">
    <h1>About</h1>
    <p class="lead">Find, adapt and copy the right shell command in under 10 seconds.</p>
  </header>

  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      GrepMeIfYouCan is a search engine for the shell commands Linux, infrastructure and DevOps
      engineers use every day. Search in plain words, edit the <strong>highlighted values</strong>,
      copy. Every command has a danger level, and destructive ones ask for a confirmation before
      the first copy.
    </p>

    <h2 id="tldr">Commands adapted from tldr-pages</h2>
    <p>
      Many commands are adapted from <a href={TLDR} rel="noopener">tldr-pages</a>, a collection of
      simplified and community-driven man pages by the tldr-pages contributors, licensed under
      the <a href={CC_BY} rel="noopener">Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License
      (CC BY 4.0)</a>. Each adapted command links to its tldr-pages source page. Changes made:
      each example became its own card, with a new title and description, editable values and a
      danger level.
    </p>

    <h2 id="licenses">Licenses</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Commands</strong> (titles, descriptions, commands): CC BY 4.0, see <a href={`${REPO_URL}/blob/main/CONTENT_LICENSE`} rel="noopener">CONTENT_LICENSE</a>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Source code</strong>: MIT, see <a href={`${REPO_URL}/blob/main/LICENSE`} rel="noopener">LICENSE</a>.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="contribute">Contribute</h2>
    <p>
      Missing a command? <a href={suggestCommandUrl()} rel="noopener">Suggest a command</a>.
      Something wrong on a command? Use <strong>Report an issue</strong> on its page. Both open a
      prefilled form on <a href={REPO_URL} rel="noopener">GitHub</a>. Nothing is published
      without a review: every change goes through a pull request.
    </p>

    <p>
      Your data stays in your browser: see <a href="/privacy">Privacy</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
